Smart Gates, Dynamic Parking and Safety Buffers (SGSB) v4.2
Quick Reference Guide — "Major Fleet & Physics Optimization Release"

Target Environment: American Truck Simulator (ATS) v1.60+

Target Master File Paths:

    /unit/hookup/animated_gate.sii

    /unit/hookup/animated_gate.dlc_*.sii (State DLC Overrides)

    /unit/hookup/parked_vehicle.sii (Fleet & Parking Density)

Compatibility: ATS Base Map, All State DLCs, & Major Map Combos (ProMods / Reforma)

[1] Core Parameter Standards — Gates & Colliders

    Universal High-Speed Approach Range: Locked to 125.0m across Illinois (dlc_il), New Mexico (dlc_nm), and Texas (dlc_tx) panorama, underground, and construction fence gates.

    Extended Trailer Clearance Range (Oregon): 135.0m (metal_01 heavy metal storage door) to prevent late-opening trailer tail-swing clipping.

    Pneumatic & Short-Range Industrial Range: Increased to 17.0m across Kansas (ag_ks_salt, ag_ks_air), Montana (ag_mt_gfll), Oklahoma (ag_pf_busf), and Wyoming (ag_wy_mine, ag_wy_ref).

    Guard-Check / Security Range: 20.0m (Borders, Ports, Mines).

    Stop-and-Go Range: 25.0m (River Locks, Floodgates). Note: Toll booths and scale actions have been reverted to stock/vanilla parameters to prevent native gate and toll-exit operational breakage.

    Collider Geometry Enforcement: Explicit .pmc physical collider file verification (ag_nv_wstg and ag_suncrops).

[2] Massive Industry & Prefab Expansion (Sections 10–48 — v4.2 New Addition)

    Industrial & Supply Chains: Granular, sector-specific configuration blocks deployed for agriculture depots, construction yards, energy logistics, chemical transport, refrigerated cold chains, intermodal containers, and timber operations.

    Municipal & Emergency: Dedicated spawn categories for fire and rescue, military defense, Department of Transportation (DOT) maintenance, border patrol, school buses, and heavy wreckers.

    Roadside & Regional Outposts: Populated truck stop diners, scenic lookouts, boat ramps, RV campgrounds, scale houses, and farm co-op lots with matching local traffic profiles.

[3] Dynamic Parking & Fleet Density Optimizations (v4.2 Enhancements)

    Deterministic Shift Weights: Cleaned up to strict separation (active shift 1.5, inactive shift 0.0 or reduced nocturnal ratios).

    Yard Trailers (Section 38): Tuned daytime weight to 1.6 and night to 0.6 with mandatory rear_align: true to ensure assets lock securely onto pads without floating.

    Lighting Flares: Standardized forced_flare_low_beam: true across all operational night-shift variants.

    Low-Poly Architecture: Overhauled background and shift-based vehicle variants across all core sections by switching low_poly_only from false to true alongside always_visible: false to eliminate VRAM spikes and stutter during heavy map mod loading.

    Render Distance Optimization: Integrated engine parameter uset g_lod_factor_parked "1.1" to pull background culling distances out just far enough to catch assets before entering the immediate field of view.

[4] Group Structure Index & Category Standards

    Group 1 & 2 (Toll Booths): Maintained at stock engine configuration to preserve toll gate functionality.
        *minus guarded toll arms at yards 25m*
    Group 3: Base Map & Western/Mountain Expansions (125.0m standard / 17.0m pneumatic).

    Group 4: Directional Rotary / Swing Gates & Heavy Doors (125.0m rotary / 135.0m Oregon metal_01).

    Group 5: Midwest & Illinois DLC Expansions (125.0m IL/MO/IA/NE / 17.0m KS).

    Group 6: Southern DLC Expansions & Depots (17.0m depot / 125.0m TX Panoramas).

    Group 7: Special Dynamic Movers & Bridge Gates (25.0m range / 100° orientation / /sound/world/gate_iron.soundref).

    Group 8: Secure Industrial Sites, Mines, Refineries & Ports (20.0m range / 90° orientation).

    Group 9: Future State Frameworks (North Dakota, Indiana, South Dakota integration).
